==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|infect|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|infectus|lang=la}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|inficiō||dye, taint}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛkt|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To bring into contact with a substance that causes illness (a [[pathogen]]).
#* {{quote-magazine|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katie-l-burke Katie L. Burke]
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/3/in-the-news-45 In the News]
|volume=101|issue=3|page=193|magazine={{w|American Scientist}}
|passage=Bats host many high-profile viruses that can '''infect''' humans, including severe acute respiratory syndrome and Ebola.}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To make somebody enthusiastic about one's own passion.
#: {{usex|Her passion for dancing has '''infected''' me.|lang=en}}

====Antonyms====
* [[disinfect]]

====Derived terms====
* [[infection]]
* [[infectible]]

====Related terms====
* [[infectious]]

